<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n113460" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χάρων</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ᾰ]</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ωνος</span>, ὁ, ἡ,
		poet. for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χαροπός, Μήνης παῖδα
		χάρωνα,</span> of the Nemean lion, <i><span class="en">
			Euph.
			84.4
		</span></i>; so as Subst. (said to be <i><span class="en">
			Maced.
		</span></i>), <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χάρωνος ὠμηστοῦ δορά</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Lyc.
					455
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>, etc.; also of <i>the eagle,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Lyc.
				260
			</span></i>; of the Cyclops, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				660
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> as pr. n.,
				<i>Charon,</i> the ferryman of the Styx, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Alc.</u>
				254
			</span></i> (lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				361
			</span></i>, al.; voc. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὦ Χάρον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Cratin.
					324c
				</span></i>
			 (
				v.l.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Χάρων</span>
			); but <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χαῖρ᾽ ὦ Χάρων</span> (with
			a pun) <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ra.</u>
				184
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
